    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40806" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί-σημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>device</i> on a coin, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				157
			</span></i>; on a shield, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὐπίσημ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					659
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἔχων . . ἐν μέσῳ σάκει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1107
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				1125
			</span></i>: also in form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί-σᾱμα</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				<u>Schwyzer</u>
				607
			</span></i> (Thess., <span class="entity">v B.C.</span>).</div>
